model CreateGatewayQuotaRuleSubjectUsageExportTaskRequest {
  gatewayId?: string(name='gatewayId', description='The gateway ID. Required. Specifies the gateway for which to export consumption details.', example='gw-123456', position='Path'),
  ruleId?: string(name='ruleId', description='The quota rule ID. Required. The rule must belong to the gateway specified by gatewayId.', example='qr-123456', position='Path'),
  subjectId?: string(name='subjectId', description='The consumption subject ID. Required. Pass the consumer ID with the cs- prefix for consumer rules, and the consumer group ID with the csg- prefix for consumer group rules. When you create a task, the subject must be bound to the specified rule, and the subject type must match the rule.', example='cs-123456', position='Path'),
  clientToken?: string(name='clientToken', description='An optional token used for request idempotency. The maximum length is 128 bytes after leading and trailing whitespaces are removed. Use ASCII characters.

When the same user retries with the same token and request parameters in the current region, the existing task is reused and its current status is returned. If the same token corresponds to different parameters, a parameter error is returned. The compared parameters include gatewayId, ruleId, subjectId, filterFailedRequests, format, and whether startTime and endTime are passed and their values. Omitting the time is not equivalent to explicitly passing 0.

Reusing a task does not recalculate the time range or regenerate the file. When you need to re-export data, including when the original task fails or the file expires, use a new token.', example='usage-export-20260729-001', position='Body'),
  endTime?: long(name='endTime', description='The end time of the export time range. Use a non-negative UNIX timestamp in seconds. This time is exclusive.

If only endTime is specified, one rule period before this time is deduced as the startTime. If neither is specified, the end time is the task creation time. If both are specified, endTime must be greater than or equal to startTime, and the span cannot exceed one rule period.', example='1783935200', position='Body'),
  filterFailedRequests?: boolean(name='filterFailedRequests', description='Specifies whether to export only consumption details with valid usage. Default value: false.

- false: Does not filter records by usage.
- true: Filters records with zero usage based on the token or credit metering dimension of the rule, and retains only records with usage.', example='true', position='Body'),
  format?: string(name='format', description='The export file format. Only CSV_GZIP is supported. If omitted or an empty string is passed, this format is used by default. The file is a GZIP-compressed CSV file named {taskId}.csv.gz. Decompress the file before reading.', example='CSV_GZIP', position='Body'),
  startTime?: long(name='startTime', description='The start time of the export time range. Use a non-negative UNIX timestamp in seconds. This time is inclusive.

- If neither startTime nor endTime is specified: The start point of the current rule period to the task creation time is used.
- If only startTime is specified: One rule period after this time is deduced as the endTime.
- If both are specified: endTime must be greater than or equal to startTime, and the span cannot exceed one rule period.

The actual export start point is also limited by the rule creation time, rule reset, or the effective start point of clearing history records. You can confirm this by querying the effectiveWindowStart returned by the task.', example='1783931600', position='Body'),
}

model CreateGatewayQuotaRuleSubjectUsageExportTaskResponseBody = {
  code?: string(name='code', description='The status code.', example='200'),
  data?: {
    status?: string(name='status', description='The current status of create task. Valid values:

- Pending: Create task is submitted and waiting to be processed.
- Running: The system is querying details, generating the file, or uploading the file.
- Success: The export is successful. Call the query operation to obtain the file information.
- Failed: The export failed. Call the query operation to view the errorMessage.

A newly created task returns Pending. When an existing task is reused through clientToken, the current status of create task is returned, which is not guaranteed to be Pending.', example='Pending'),
    taskId?: string(name='taskId', description='The export task ID. When you call GetGatewayQuotaRuleSubjectUsageExportTask, pass this value along with the gatewayId, ruleId, and subjectId from this request.', example='finops-export-abcdef1234567890'),
  }(name='data', description='The response data.', example='{
  "taskId": "finops-export-abcdef1234567890",
  "status": "Pending"
}'),
  message?: string(name='message', description='The response message.', example='success'),
  requestId?: string(name='requestId', description='The request ID of this OpenAPI call, which is used to troubleshoot call issues. This is different from the request_id of each consumption record in the exported file.', example='1234567890'),
}

model CreateGatewayQuotaRuleSubjectUsageExportTaskResponse = {
  headers?: map[string]string(name='headers'),
  statusCode?: int32(name='statusCode'),
  body?: CreateGatewayQuotaRuleSubjectUsageExportTaskResponseBody(name='body'),
}

/**
  * @description ## Procedure
  * This operation creates an export task for the consumption details of a consumer or consumer group under a specified gateway quota rule. The exported content is sourced from gateway access logs.
  * 1. Call this operation to obtain the taskId. A new task returns Pending, which indicates that the task is submitted and the file is not yet generated.
  * 2. Call GetGatewayQuotaRuleSubjectUsageExportTask with the same gatewayId, ruleId, subjectId, and the returned taskId to poll the task status.
  * 3. When the polled status is Success and the file has not expired, download the csv.gz file by using GetGatewayQuotaRuleSubjectUsageExportTask. If the status is Failed, troubleshoot the issue based on the errorMessage and recreate the task.
  * ## Prerequisites and limits
  * - When you create a task, the quota rule must exist, and the target subject must be bound to the rule. Use the consumer ID for consumer rules and the consumer group ID for consumer group rules.
  * - The details within the valid export time range depend on the delivery of gateway access logs. Enable log delivery first and ensure that the logs for the required time period are queryable.
  * - The time span for a single export cannot exceed one rule period. A single export can contain up to 100,000 details. If the background statistics exceed this limit, the task fails. Narrow the time range and try again.
  * - If the same user already has a Pending or Running task for the same gateway, rule, and subject in the current region within the last 10 minutes, repeated creation is rejected. Creation is also rejected if the total number of export tasks created within the last 10 minutes that are still Pending or Running reaches three. Wait for the existing tasks to complete. Idempotent retries with the same clientToken and parameters can reuse existing tasks.
  * - The processing timeout for a task is 10 minutes from creation. After a timeout, the task is processed as Failed. This is not a guarantee that the task will successfully complete within the time limit.
  * - The export time range, metering dimension, and subject name are determined at creation. Subsequent queries do not recalculate these conditions. After the file is successfully generated, the download link is available for 24 hours. The signed link generated for each query is valid for 10 minutes. The exact validity period is subject to the query result.
  * @param request  the request parameters of CreateGatewayQuotaRuleSubjectUsageExportTask  CreateGatewayQuotaRuleSubjectUsageExportTaskRequest
  * @return CreateGatewayQuotaRuleSubjectUsageExportTaskResponse
 */
