  conflictHash?: string(name='conflictHash', description='The conflict snapshot hash, which is used to prevent concurrent dirty overwrites when confirming an overwrite. You can obtain this value by first executing a request with dryRun=true and extracting it from the response.

You do not need to specify this parameter in the following scenarios: no conflicts exist; you are only performing a dry run with dryRun=true; or overwrite=false, meaning you do not confirm the overwrite.

If dryRun=false and overwrite=true but this parameter is not provided or has expired and does not match, the backend returns accepted=false along with a new conflict preview. In this case, you must perform a dry run again to confirm the new conflicts.', example='f8f44dc6cf369a017d56b7197eb4fb5ac4bbb6b09a92b9b41999541f50xxxxxx', position='Body'),
